  "prediction": "**Lobbying Disclosure Act Compliance: Observations and Recommendations**\n\nThe Government Accountability Office (GAO) conducted a performance audit to assess the compliance of lobbyists with the Lobbying Disclosure Act (LDA) of 1995, as amended. The audit aimed to determine the extent to which lobbyists demonstrate compliance with reporting requirements, identify challenges and potential improvements to compliance, and describe the resources and authorities available to the U.S. Attorney's Office (USAO) for enforcing LDA compliance.\n\n**Key Findings:**\n\n1. **Compliance with Reporting Requirements:** The audit found that 87.2% of newly filed registrations were matched with corresponding disclosure reports, indicating a high level of compliance with the LDA's requirement for lobbyists to file reports in the quarter of registration.\n2. **Documentation of Income and Expenses:** The audit found that 99% of LD-2 reports provided written documentation for income and expenses, a statistically significant increase from 2016.\n3. **Rounding of Income and Expenses:** The audit found that 25% of reports did not round reported income or expenses according to the guidance, a recurring issue since 2010.\n4. **Disclosure of Covered Positions:** The audit found that 15% of LD-2 reports may not have properly disclosed previously held covered positions as required.\n5. **LD-203 Reports:** The audit found that 12% of LD-203 reports failed to disclose one or more reportable contributions, and 53% of referrals are pending further action due to the inability to locate the lobbyist or lack of response.\n\n**Challenges to Compliance:**\n\n1. **Difficulty in Locating Lobbyists:** The audit found that USAO has difficulty pursuing LD-203 referrals for lobbyists who have departed a firm without leaving forwarding contact information.\n2. **Complexity of LD-203 Reports:** The audit found that LD-203 reports are more complicated than LD-2 reports, making it challenging for lobbyists to comply with the requirements.\n\n**Recommendations:**\n\n1. **Improve Guidance:** The GAO recommends that the Secretary of the Senate and the Clerk of the House improve guidance on the LDA to clarify the requirements for lobbyists and lobbying firms.\n2. **Enhance Enforcement:** The GAO recommends that USAO enhance its enforcement efforts to focus on chronic offenders and improve its tracking system to monitor compliance trends and referrals.\n3. **Simplify LD-203 Reports:** The GAO recommends that the LDA be amended to simplify LD-203 reports and reduce the complexity of the reporting",
